Darwin: panfrost for the Metal driver (userland/a34metal).

From HackiOS's Mali Metal driver (MIT, Copyright 2026 Darwin on redwood contributors;
github.com/oosexgang/hakios-xnu-kernel, branch mtk, tools/mesa/panfrost-darwin.patch and
panfrost-redwood-perf.patch), ported to Mesa 26.3 and to Valhall:

- counters of batch submissions and draw-time shader variants that air_metal.c reads
  (rwa_submit_profile);
- 256 bytes of slack after every transient pool allocation (their G52's fragment preload
  wrote past one);
- no transaction elimination (CRC) on Darwin: IOSurface memory changes behind a resource;
- 16-bit UBO loads widened to 32-bit, for the Metal driver's shaders only (label "air";
  boot-arg widen16=0 turns it off).

Not taken (performance only, to come once the Metal path draws right): pushing every UBO
(pushubo) with panfrost_emit_const_buf reading resource-backed UBOs, and a shader's scratch
arrays into registers (scratchregs). Their Bifrost-v7-only build switches are not taken
either: our build keeps every architecture panfrost has.

